  "map_id": "map:pierre-auger-observatory",
  "method": "The 49 active stations that sdMap.csv flags sd750 = 1 but not sd1500 (the 22 that are in both arrays are drawn with the main array). Station positions are the northing and easting columns of sdMap.csv in the Pierre Auger Collaboration Open Data release 3 (20 March 2024, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.10488964), which the Collaboration describes as \"UTC\" [sic] coordinates in metres (the data page does not state the zone or datum). They are read as UTM zone 19 south (central meridian 69 deg W) on the WGS 84 ellipsoid (EPSG:32719) because only zone 19 puts the numbers at Malargue (the converted stations span latitude 34.93 to 35.52 S and longitude 68.91 to 69.66 W), and WGS 84 is the GPS datum; this reading is this work's assumption, hence confidence approximate and accuracy_m 50. Only stations the release marks as still in operation (stop = 1) are drawn; 53 stations with a recorded stop time are not. Each station is drawn as a 3.6 m square centred on its position, aligned to true north: the tank diameter of 3.6 m is from the Observatory paper (arXiv:1502.01323 section 3.1), so the marker has the real tank size, not the tank outline. Check: nearest-neighbour distance of the 71 active sd750 stations has a median of 742.7 m against the official 750 m spacing (arXiv:1502.01323 abstract).",
